    "revision": 1,
    "title": "Learn a communication strategy",
    "subtitle": "Solving a practical problem",
    "context": "Describe actions affecting particular objects and events affecting people.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-CORE-U28-skill-K-HSK3-pragmatics-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "HSK 3: pragmatics",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Naming an affected person does not by itself prove blame or intention. Describe the stated event first and request missing context before assigning responsibility.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "被",
                "pinyin": "bèi",
                "meaning": "marks an action done to someone or something",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "c0d59c368ade50e2bab9f6bc2c1aabee0b378b23c17a90872aa2058086324354"
              },
              {
                "text": "对不起",
                "pinyin": "duìbuqǐ",
                "meaning": "sorry",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "70793902a26c9a6674a77d286ad9de4025f3b0b0b7c66447408967470dd22456"
              },
              {
                "text": "谢谢",
                "pinyin": "xièxie",
                "meaning": "thank you",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "77c9dcfb11bca11b415da7602e960e26a88db99372c35891d5ceccad29b06263"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A cup belonging to a partner was broken. The affected partner reports the broken cup but does not say whether the action was deliberate or who performed it. Describe the effect and ask what happened before assigning blame.\nFamiliar meanings available: marks an action done to someone or something; sorry; thank you."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EX-CORE-U28-skill-K-HSK3-pragmatics-perform",
        "kind": "check",
        "title": "Use the skill in context",
